--- caveats for orch ---
1. The xmod_attn_v0 numbers come from T0022 which has human_ack_needed=true on
   the latency trigger. If orch decides to retry T0022 with v1 (more parallel
   DSPs), those numbers change AND so does the xmod_attn row of this budget.
   Worst case under T0022 v1 (4x parallel t-loop): DSP 12 → 48, LUT 13272 → ~25k.
   xmod_attn P_dyn would rise to ~0.30 W. New total ≈ 6.03 W. Still passes.

2. The two PROJECTED modules (GVSA matmul, action diff head) carry MUCH more
   uncertainty than the ±25% confidence band implies. The band is for the
   measurement model; the projection numbers themselves have ~50% uncertainty.
   These should be replaced with real synth numbers when those modules are
   built (TBD task IDs).

3. Tag in paper: [HLS-EST]+[HIPPO]+[partial-projection]. Don't claim a
   measured power number until vivado_pnr + report_power is done.

CONCLUSION: MR-VLA power budget = 5.84 W ± 25% (worst case 7.30 W) — well
under the 30 W plan cap and well under typical Jetson Orin AGX operating
power. W1 spike S1.6 closes cleanly; no risk flagged.
